MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I figured out a way to go about it.  Basically, I pre-calculate the batch timeout a column in the pallet arrivals dataframe.  I then set a global using that column with each pallet's arrival.  Because every pallet in the same truck has the same value in the batch timeout column of the dataframe, the last value of the global, prior to the batch proceeding, is the global value that is then used for the batch's timeout.

Not ideal, since I have to pre-calculate the timeout rather than calculating it inside the simulation by getting the batch size, but it works for what I need.

Stripped-down version.
https://github.com/datadrivensupplychain/teaching_bits/blob/main/batch_unload_time_simulation.r

Ralph
ra...@datadrivensupplychain.com

